WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.260
A new superhero might be about&nbsp;
to land in the DC Universe — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:07.080
are fans feeling terrific about&nbsp;
this new addition… or terrible?

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.460
James Gunn continues to stir speculation&nbsp;
about the future of his DC Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:15.600
having now tweeted a captionless photo&nbsp;
of the superhero Mister Terrific. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:20.040
character is well known to comic book fans as a&nbsp;
brilliant mind capable of competing with Bruce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:24.480
Wayne's skills of detection, strategy, and&nbsp;
engineering. He was a significant part of DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:28.920
Comics' universe-wide "Futures End" story&nbsp;
arc during the New 52 era, and recently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.540
served as the primary antagonist of Tom King's&nbsp;
Black Label maxi-series Strange Adventures.

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.980
Black Adam's Hawkman actor Aldis Hodge&nbsp;
recently told GamesRadar that he'd like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.980
to do a team-up film featuring both&nbsp;
his character and Mister Terrific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:45.420
with his brother, Edwin Hodge, reprising&nbsp;
the role from the 2021 film Injustice.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.360
The character has been voiced by&nbsp;
numerous actors over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:53.220
from Michael Beach in Justice League Unlimited to&nbsp;
comedian Hannibal Buress in Justice League Action.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.720
"Saved by the bell. It’s time to T up."

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:03.780
The character made his live-action debut in&nbsp;
the TV series Arrow, played by Echo Kellum.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.400
"Nice aim."
"That’s the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.800
thing, they aim themselves."

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:17.400
Gunn's photo comes from an early 2000s issue&nbsp;
of Justice Society of America, illustrated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.680
by legendary comic book artist Alex Ross, and it&nbsp;
has sparked countless casting theories from fans.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.580
One Twitter user suggested The Good&nbsp;
Place star William Jackson Harper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:30.480
an actor who recently made superhero&nbsp;
headlines after his casting in Ant-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.200
Quantumania led to rumors that he&nbsp;
would play the MCU's Mister Fantastic.

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:38.940
"Put the Peeps in the chili&nbsp;
pot, it makes it taste… bad…"

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:42.780
Coming off the back of the final season&nbsp;
of Atlanta, another Twitter user wrote:

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:44.940
"Lakeith Stanfield please James!!!"

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:50.040
Another user suggested Jonathan Majors,&nbsp;
who recently made his MCU debut in Loki&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.400
and is set to play the franchise's&nbsp;
next big bad: Kang the Conqueror.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:02.400
"Not every version of me&nbsp;
was so, so pure of heart."

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:06.420
Meanwhile, one Twitter user suggested&nbsp;
This Is Us actor Sterling K. Brown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:09.900
Brown recently starred in the film&nbsp;
Honk For Jesus. Save Your Soul,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:15.240
but is more widely known to superhero fans as the&nbsp;
brother of King T'Chaka in 2018's Black Panther.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.500
Gunn has been relatively open about his&nbsp;
role as the new co-head of the DC Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.060
seemingly eager to reassure fans that their wishes&nbsp;
will be considered under his leadership. Still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.380
the question of Mister Terrific is a tricky&nbsp;
one. While he's definitely a popular character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.580
he's also a member of an ensemble and not&nbsp;
considered one of the "main" characters in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.960
DC universe. Many fans were excited about the&nbsp;
potential for more projects about the Justice&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.520
Society of America, but some were apprehensive&nbsp;
about the idea of DC jumping straight into a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:45.780
Mr. Terrific project without establishing&nbsp;
him in another film. One user suggested:

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:50.700
"Set up [the main characters], then start working&nbsp;
on DC's large list of other characters to add in."

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:53.640
All in all, fans' reaction&nbsp;
to Gunn's post seems to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.940
a mixture of excitement that their favorite&nbsp;
character might be adapted for the screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:02.100
and concern that the filmmakers might screw&nbsp;
it up. Such is the life of a comic book fan.

